From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:55:04 +0000
Subject: clk: sunxi-ng: h616: register GPU PLL notifier before mux notifier

Register the GPU PLL notifier first, so the GPU goes back to the PLL
only after it has re-locked. Commit 0ec5e7572ddc ("clk: sunxi-ng: h616:
register CPU PLL notifier before mux notifier") did this for the CPU.

Fixes: eb963d7948ce ("clk: sunxi-ng: h616: Reparent GPU clock during frequency changes")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
index 2893751..5b30e1c 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
@@ -1266,13 +1266,16 @@ static int sun50i_h616_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ccu_mux_notifier_register(pll_cpux_clk.common.hw.clk,
 				  &sun50i_h616_cpu_nb);
 
+	/*
+	 * Re-lock the GPU PLL after any rate changes. Must be registered
+	 * before the mux notifier, so GPU goes back to a locked PLL.
+	 */
+	ccu_pll_notifier_register(&sun50i_h616_pll_gpu_nb);
+
 	/* Reparent GPU during GPU PLL rate changes */
 	ccu_mux_notifier_register(pll_gpu_clk.common.hw.clk,
 				  &sun50i_h616_gpu_nb);
 
-	/* Re-lock the GPU PLL after any rate changes */
-	ccu_pll_notifier_register(&sun50i_h616_pll_gpu_nb);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
